WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.603 line:92%
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:07.273
And, by the way, it's lovely
to have you in another show

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
that takes place
in New York City.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:11.411
Excellent accent work there.
-[ New York accent] Thanks.

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:12.746 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, it was great.

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you actually
got to be in Scotland.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.016 line:92%
You were there this morning?

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:16.850 line:92%
Did you wake up in Scotland?

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yesterday morning,
I woke up in Scotland.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was there, 'cause
it was Mother's Day in Sc--

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:23.423
'Cause we have Mother's Day
on a different day from you.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:23.823 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Really?

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:24.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're panicking
that you missed it.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I would've.
I definitely would've.

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, we have Mother's Day
on Sundays.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.463
I saw my mom, and I was at
a wedding, a lovely wedding.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.700
And my friends got married
at St Andrews on Saturday.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
And before that,
I was filming a bit,

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:39.806
and it was also my mum's
80th birthday last month.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.074 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, fantastic.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:41.775 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:45.211
Was she -- She must have just
been delighted, I'm assuming,

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have you home
for her birthday.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:47.614 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. It was good.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:50.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
And actually all of my family
who are alive were there.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.419 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I do want you to know

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:55.155 size:78% position:39%
that we wouldn't have
thought otherwise.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wouldn't have
followed up with,

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:57.957 line:92%
"Even the dead ones, Alan?"

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:58.691 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Even the dead ones.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.561
We have old Scottish traditions,
but that's not one of them.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:06.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you get to play
a retired CIA operative.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:06.766 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...who gets recruited
by the NYPD...

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:09.169 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:11.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...because a serial killer
is using your book.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My book which
I've written, uh-huh.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.407 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And I'm also sort of a

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:17.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
fuddy-duddy professor
at Penn State.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-There's a lot going on.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.847
-There's a lot going on.
-And also I'm a homosexual.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:21.915 line:92%
-Yeah, which is very exciting.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to
just roll by that.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.885 line:92%
Because it's not the most --

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not what your
character's about.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. See, that's what I think
is great about it, Seth,

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:30.857 size:75% position:38% line:92%
is that it's like --

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:33.326
The fourth or fifth thing
of the characteristics

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
of this person
is that he's gay and married

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a happy, you know,
solid marriage.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
And actually what I think
is really amazing

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:40.767 line:92%
is that most of the times,

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially on network TV,
when someone is gay,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:45.438
when there's a gay character,
it's like they're gay, gay, gay!

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's all about
their sexuality,

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.341 line:92%
and usually in a negative way.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the fact that
this has a character

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
whose gayness is way down
the list of things

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:55.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are most important
about him is a positive thing.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
And also the fact that
when you do see

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of his same-sex life,
it's in a really positive way.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's two things
I don't think

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:03.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
are represented enough
in this country.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:06.226 size:84% position:42%
-Well, it's fantastic.
And I didn't realize --

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:07.527 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:10.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
The first --
It's the first time.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:14.901
-It's the first time on a
network drama that a gay --

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.935 size:84% position:42% line:92%
there's been a TV drama

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.770 size:75% position:38%
with a gay character
in the leading role.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's amazing.
-It's shocking.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Perfect.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:25.912
You -- Obviously, this is
a show about the police.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:28.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're a CIA operative.
So you have a gun.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do have a gun, yes,
which has been --

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:33.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's sort of, uh --
Well, I mean --

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.822
I have mixed feelings about that
because I'm very --

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:38.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
I play sort of a cop person
and a CIA person.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
So obviously he has a gun.
It's part of the story.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:43.997
But obviously -- And especially
in the current atmosphere,

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:48.101
I have -- it's difficult for me
to kind of marry that.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
I think it's really hard

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:53.706
for people in this country
who are so used to gun violence

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
just being
an everyday occurrence

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:57.677 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and sort of almost an

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
unacceptable part
of your culture.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:02.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
From where I'm from,
there was never any idea

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.583 size:81% position:41% line:92%
of people owning guns.

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's been difficult for me,
but I have it.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.321 line:92%
But, you know, I'm quite --

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't really
ever shoot anyone,

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:13.760
but the only thing I've ever --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
In the show, I mean.
The only time -- [ Laughs ]

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
The only time
I've ever shot anything

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:21.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
is I shot a glass
of poisoned iced tea

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.403 line:92%
out of Whoopi Goldberg's hand.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-Thereby saving her life.

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.208
And, also, I'm really bad
'cause there's always those

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:30.944 size:84% position:42%
lovely cop adviser guys
and gun adviser people

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:33.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
who show you how to grip it
and everything.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I -- I'm, like,
the lead in the show,

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I guess they don't
really say to me,

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.486 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"Uh, that was rubbish."

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I realized after
the first couple of times

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:45.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
that my co-star Bojana,
she's quite small.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.962
And the first time we come in
and go, "Police," or whatever,

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
I realized that
she was taller than me,

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:56.502
and it's because my stance for
doing the gun, I go like this.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.503 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Like sort of --

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like Broadway, Bob Fosse
kind of thing.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.008 line:92%
She's so much taller than me

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause my legs
are so wide apart.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
And someone said,
"Why do you do that?"

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:07.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "I don't know. I didn't
realize I was doing it."

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe just to be balanced,
you know?

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:10.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that's --
So I'm kind of a --

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:14.320
I've got a sort of slight
Broadway flair to my...

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.156 line:92%
[ Laughs ] As you should.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

